  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every integer n >= 1, let L_n be Shoji's two-bridge link C(1^(2n+1)) and let P_n be its Q-polynomial after removal of its Laurent monomial factor, exactly as fixed in problem.md. Every zero of P_n is real; in fact, every zero is simple and lies in [-3,1]. Thus the frozen universal assertion in source.md is proved in its full scope.",
